# a double read by INPUT # is read as a double (the 1983 source's FILIND, 6/27/80: FINDBL); PC-BASIC reads 1E+20 as a single, then makes it double; and (the IBM manual's pp. 133-134, the fix-up's review round 1, F1) INPUT # passes over leading CRs and LFs, so line 50's empty line is no item: the quoted string is line 150's first (PC-BASIC reads it as an empty item)
["plain",1,-2.5,"with, comma"]
["",0]
[]
["quoted "part",12,"end"]
[1E+20,.3333334,-.3333333333333333]
<plain> 1 -2.5 <with, comma>
<> 0 
<quoted ><part"><12><end>
 1D+20  .3333334 -.3333333333333333 
-1 
